---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Nav from '../components/Nav.astro';
import SiteFooter from '../components/SiteFooter.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
	title="About"
	description="Ohana Tech helps regulated businesses adopt AI with governance built in. Founded by Tim McCrimmon."
>
	<Nav />

	<div class="about-page">
		<div class="about-prose">
			<p class="section-label">About</p>
			<h1>Ohana Tech</h1>
			<p class="subtitle">Pragmatic AI for regulated industries</p>

			<p>
				Ohana Tech helps regulated businesses put AI to work without losing control of their data,
				their compliance obligations, or their costs. Our clients build medical devices and provide
				financing to small businesses. What they share is that a mistake in how AI is used carries
				consequences well beyond a bad answer.
			</p>

			<p>
				We start with governance because it's what lets AI scale. Once a company knows what AI may touch,
				who is accountable for its output, and how that will be shown to an auditor or a customer, the
				question of where AI adds value gets much easier to answer, and much easier to act on.
			</p>

			<h2>How we work</h2>
			<p>
				Engagements are led directly by Tim McCrimmon, with delivery by Ohana's engineering team of AI
				specialists in the United States and Serbia. Senior AI engineers and researchers join projects when
				the work calls for them.
			</p>
			<p>
				We develop our core technology in the open. The <a href="https://structuredcontext.dev" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Structured
				Context Specification</a> is published under Apache 2.0, so clients can see exactly how their
				governance is represented rather than taking it on trust.
			</p>

			<h2>Tim McCrimmon, Founder</h2>
			<p>
				Tim has spent his career building technology in environments where reliability and accountability
				are part of the job, from naval shipbuilding to enterprise software to healthcare data exchange.
			</p>

			<h3>Optum / UnitedHealth Group</h3>
			<p>
				Eight years as a technology executive for advanced clinical solutions. Tim designed and built
				<strong>Calypso</strong>, an internal platform for multi-EHR integration using FHIR and SMART on FHIR,
				which gave clinical and administrative applications access to patient data across health systems
				without a separate integration contract for each. He led Optum's technical engagement on
				<strong>21st Century Cures</strong> compliance, contributed to AI-driven clinical decision support,
				and was the lead technology executive for prior authorization guidance initiatives.
			</p>

			<h3>Red Hat</h3>
			<p>
				Architect and designer for embedded systems, OpenStack, and OpenShift (Docker/Kubernetes). This is
				the cloud-native infrastructure that now runs AI workloads in production, and it informs how Ohana
				designs private AI deployments.
			</p>

			<h3>IBM</h3>
			<p>
				Software Development Product Manager across IBM's software portfolio. Tim conceived and drove the
				decision to <strong>open source Eclipse</strong>, which shaped his view of open standards as a way to
				build ecosystems that outlast any single vendor.
			</p>

			<h3>Lenovo</h3>
			<p>
				Product Manager for ThinkPad Accessories, including secure external storage, adapter cables, and
				USB-C implementations: hardware and software integration across the full product lifecycle, from
				specification to manufacturing.
			</p>

			<h3>U.S. Navy</h3>
			<p>
				Naval service, followed by program management for shipbuilding with the Department of the Navy.
			</p>

			<h3>Education</h3>
			<p>
				<strong>B.S., Electrical Engineering</strong> — Rutgers University<br />
				<strong>M.S. Certificate, Healthcare Informatics</strong> — Boston University
			</p>
		</div>

